riddle: 0 ~ 1/2 = 3/4: lit at 0:00:00 and 0:30:00, gone at 0:45:00. Made with 2 fuses in all: (0 ~ (0 ~ 0)). The first fuse, lit at both ends, measured the half hour; the second was lit at one end at the start and at the other when the first went out. || chips: 0 0:00:00, 1/2 0:30:00, 3/4 0:45:00
wild: 8449/4096 = 19/16 ~ 3969/2048, gone at 2:03:45.878…, with 13 fuses. The simple recipe (the procedure M) goes from 33/16 straight to 4225/2048 and never makes this number, which lies between them. The paper calls it the smallest wild number its authors know of. || 14 chips
first and last chip: A fuse lit at 0 is gone by 1 at the latest; at 8449/4096 there is nothing left to light. The two ends must be lit less than an hour apart.
